From 1ab81ca9da7160065d274ae58f574e78b94d5f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AdrianProk <Prokopczyk.Adrian@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:42:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] 3DS: Show the hotel map with the current room on the
 top screen (MAUSJAGD_PORT)

Standalone build of "Mausejagd im Grandhotel": once the game has shown
its hotel overview (movie GGMDMENU), the top screen shows that hotel
map scaled to 320x240, a blinking frame around the room the player is
in and the number of caught mice (Lingo global miceCaught). Before
that, the top screen shows the game as before.

- OSystem::setSecondaryScreen(): new optional backend call, a no-op by
  default, implemented by the 3DS backend (top screen picture plus a
  blinking marker; the backend magnify mode still shows the game)
- Director: mausjagdSecondaryScreenTick() in the main loop takes the
  overview picture with its own palette, the room names from field
  "roomlist" and the outlines of the room pictures. The room sprites
  are the hot spots of the mouse detector and lie lower than the
  pictures, so the outlines of the known picture are a measured table;
  other pictures fall back to the sprites.
- "mausjagd_debug_room" in scummvm.ini pretends to be in a room, for
  tests without input

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
